  "razonamiento": "The architecture shows SonarSource's code analysis and reporting platform. DEVELOPERS is mapped to UserConsumerDeveloper. GitHub is a ThirdParty service triggering a Lambda on code push, which feeds an SQS queue. A worker ECS Fargate task pulls from SQS, fetches repository code, and writes results to Aurora. Developers also submit reports directly to an EC2 instance. Another ECS Fargate service ('Compute Engine') pulls reports from Aurora and indexes them into Elasticsearch (OpenSearch). Spoken mentions of users/UI/API are omitted as they are conversational and not drawn on the board. The two duplicate visual lines between Compute Engine and Aurora are merged into a single polling edge.",
